{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":97323,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"531bfb79d3d6c7812b0e7bc7435b6be91b14ebb97066b762b4413687a699af98","packTokens":57658,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":307,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"drafts","tokens":57323,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"merge"},"pointers":[],"system":"Merge three independent spec drafts into one spec (same format rules as the drafts).\nEvery merged requirement lists in \"alignment\" which draft requirements it came from, as \"d<draft>:<REQ-id>\" (e.g. \"d1:REQ-2\"). Keep a requirement even if only one draft has it. Never write a requirement that is in no draft.\nWhen drafts conflict, keep both readings as separate requirements and add a conflict entry. Renumber merged requirements REQ-1.. and their ACs AC-<req>.<n>.\nEach Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes. Reword a draft's Then that doesn't, without changing what it checks.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"drafts\" kind=\"spec-drafts\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d1\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"The business rules live in one booking service module with public methods (book, joinWaitlist, cancel, leaveWaitlist, undoBooking, getBookings, getStats, getActionState, simulateOtherMemberCancellation) and an injectable clock and storage, so rules can be unit-tested and are enforced outside the UI (ASM-6).\",\n   \"Booking window boundaries: a session starting exactly 168 hours from now is bookable; exactly 15 minutes before start is bookable, 14 minutes is not (Q-4).\",\n   \"Free cancellation applies when the start is at least 2 hours away; less than 2 hours is a late cancellation.\",\n   \"When Alex cancels a Booked session with an empty waitlist, the booked count drops by 1; with a waitlist, the booked count stays the same and the waitlist count drops by 1 (Q-5).\",\n   \"Joining a waitlist is rejected while spots are free.\",\n   \"Leaving a waitlist sets the record to Cancelled with no late flag, so it appears in Past as \\\"Cancelled\\\".\",\n   \"Availability labels: 1 free spot reads \\\"1 spot left\\\" (taken from the request's §11 example), 2–3 read \\\"Only N left\\\", 4 or more read \\\"N spots left\\\".\",\n   \"Filters combine as OR within a group and AND across groups; Afternoon is 12:00–16:59 and Evening is 17:00 onward (ASM-10).\",\n   \"Classes this month counts only Attended records. Streak counts consecutive Monday–Sunday weeks with at least one Attended record, counting back from the current week, or from the previous week if the current week has none yet (request §13).\",\n   \"Waitlist promotion is announced in-app with a toast the next time the app opens (request §13).\",\n   \"Because Alex is never seeded onto a studio-cancelled class and there is no staff UI, a booked class cannot become studio-cancelled in this release; if it ever did, it would show in Past as \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\" (ASM-8, ASM-19).\",\n   \"The tablet layout starts at 768 px and the desktop side-panel layout at 1024 px.\",\n   \"The static app is hosted in one cloud region in the client's cloud account (ASM-13).\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"Time from day-chip activation to cards displayed < 1000 ms on a Moto G Power–class device (or Lighthouse mid-tier mobile throttling), measured over 10 runs, p90\",\n    \"text\": \"The Schedule for a selected day renders with seed data on a mid-range phone profile.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"Button/card state change displayed ≤ 100 ms after activation, p95 over 20 actions\",\n    \"text\": \"Book, cancel, join and leave actions give visual feedback optimistically.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n    \"metric\": \"Contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 for normal text and ≥ 3:1 for large text and UI components; 0 violations in an automated axe scan of all 3 screens in both modes\",\n    \"text\": \"All text/background combinations meet WCAG 2.1 AA contrast in light and dark mode.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n    \"metric\": \"100% of interactive elements ≥ 44 × 44 px at 360 px viewport\",\n    \"text\": \"Touch targets are large enough for touch use.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n    \"metric\": \"With prefers-reduced-motion: reduce, 0 transitions or animations longer than 0 ms on card press, sheet/panel slide, capacity bar fill and toast\",\n    \"text\": \"Motion respects reduced-motion preference.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n    \"metric\": \"0 occurrences of stack traces or raw exception text on any screen across the full test suite, including forced storage failures\",\n    \"text\": \"Users never see raw errors.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n    \"metric\": \"End-to-end test passes on the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox (8 browser versions)\",\n    \"text\": \"Browser support.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n    \"metric\": \"Median time from app open to booking confirmation ≤ 30 s across 5 first-time testers\",\n    \"text\": \"Members can find and book a class quickly.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"Sign in, sign up, password reset; a single pre-signed-in demo member (request §12)\",\n   \"Payments, credits, class packs, membership purchase (request §12)\",\n   \"Staff, instructor or admin screens and schedule editing (request §12)\",\n   \"Email, SMS or push notifications (request §12)\",\n   \"Calendar export or sync (request §12)\",\n   \"Multiple studio locations (request §12)\",\n   \"Native mobile apps (request §12)\",\n   \"Multi-language support (request §12)\",\n   \"A backend server or database: persistence is browser local storage only (ASM-15, ASM-6)\",\n   \"Any visible UI for the waitlist promotion demo hook; it is test-only (ASM-16)\",\n   \"Modelling other members as individual records; they exist only as booked and waitlist counts (Q-5)\",\n   \"Schedule navigation beyond the current and next week (ASM-9, ASM-20)\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A browser with seeded data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The Schedule screen is shown, and the top bar shows the text \\\"Pulse Studio\\\" and an avatar with the text \\\"AR\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"The app root URL is opened\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The Schedule screen is shown\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The My Bookings screen is shown with the name \\\"Alex Rivera\\\" and the membership \\\"Unlimited Monthly\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"The \\\"AR\\\" avatar is activated\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking app shall present exactly three screens, Schedule (the home screen at the root URL), Class Detail and My Bookings, under a top bar that shows the \\\"Pulse Studio\\\" wordmark and the member avatar with initials \\\"AR\\\" linking to My Bookings.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A fixed clock of Wednesday 2026-10-07 10:00 Europe/London\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned session list has a count of at least 40, includes every one of the 5 class types and 3 rooms, and the returned instructor list has a count of 5, each with a name, a bio and an avatar\",\n      \"when\": \"The seed generator is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The same returned seed data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"At least 3 sessions have booked count equal to capacity, at least 3 have capacity minus booked count between 1 and 3, and at least 1 has status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"Sessions are counted by availability\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The same returned seed data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Exactly 2 records are Booked on sessions starting after now, 1 record is Waitlisted with a waitlist position value, 3 records are Attended on sessions that ended before now, and no record refers to a session with status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"Alex Rivera's booking records are read\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The same returned seed data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-2.4\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Every session has a name, type, intensity of Low/Medium/High, instructor, room, start date-time, a duration value of 30, 45, 60 or 75, capacity, booked count, waitlist count, a description and a non-empty what-to-bring list\",\n      \"when\": \"Each session's fields are read\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the seed generator runs, the booking service shall return seed data containing at least 40 class sessions across the types Yoga, Pilates, HIIT, Spin and Boxing and the rooms Studio A, Studio B and Spin Room, 5 instructors, at least 3 full sessions, at least 3 sessions with 1–3 spots left, at least 1 session with status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\", and for demo member Alex Rivera 2 upcoming Booked bookings, 1 Waitlisted booking and 3 past Attended bookings, none of them on a studio-cancelled session.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"ASM-8\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Empty local storage and a fixed clock of Wednesday 2026-10-07 10:00 Europe/London\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Every returned session start date falls between Monday 2026-10-05 00:00 and Sunday 2026-10-18 23:59 Europe/London, and local storage holds a stored record of the sessions\",\n      \"when\": \"The booking service is initialised\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Local storage already holds data seeded on 2026-10-07\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned sessions have the same IDs and start dates as the stored data\",\n      \"when\": \"The booking service is initialised with a clock of 2026-10-09\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the app loads and no stored data exists in browser local storage, the booking service shall generate the seed sessions dated within the current Monday–Sunday week and the next week, both measured from today in Europe/London, and store them so later loads reuse the stored data without regenerating it.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"ASM-5\",\n     \"ASM-20\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A booking service instance over a local storage with seeded data and a bookable session S\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The new instance's returned booking list contains a Booked record for S and the returned booked count of S is 1 higher than before\",\n      \"when\": \"book(S) succeeds and a new booking service instance is created over the same storage\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex has booked a class through the Schedule screen\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The class card button is shown as \\\"Booked ✓\\\" and the class is listed under Upcoming in My Bookings\",\n      \"when\": \"The page is reloaded\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When any booking action changes data, the booking service shall write the change to browser local storage before reporting success, so the change is returned after a page reload.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-15\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A clock of 2026-10-06T23:30Z (00:30 on 7 October in Europe/London)\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned date is 2026-10-07\",\n      \"when\": \"The booking service's today value is read\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session starting at 2026-10-07T17:30Z\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned text is \\\"18:30\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"The time formatter is called for it\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking app shall show all dates and times in the Europe/London timezone in 24-hour format and shall work out \\\"today\\\" from the Europe/London date.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Session \\\"Sunrise Vinyasa\\\" with capacity 20, booked count 18, starting in 2 days, with no conflicts\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Booked, a booking ID and a created date-time, and the session's returned booked count value is 19\",\n      \"when\": \"book(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex already holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for session S\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Only one active record for S exists in the returned booking list, the booked count rises by at most 1 in total, and the repeat call returns an \\\"already booked\\\" error\",\n      \"when\": \"book(S) is called again, including two calls in a row with no wait between them\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex books a Scheduled session that has free spots, starts within the booking window, does not overlap another Booked session of Alex's and keeps Alex at or under 10 upcoming Booked sessions, the booking service shall create one Booked record with an ID and created date-time and increase the session's booked count by 1.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Session \\\"Power HIIT\\\" with capacity 16 and booked count 16\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"class full\\\", no Booked record is created, and the booked count value stays 16\",\n      \"when\": \"book(session) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If a session's booked count equals its capacity, then the booking service shall reject a book request with a \\\"class full\\\" error and leave the booked and waitlist counts unchanged.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Session \\\"Power HIIT\\\" is full with waitlist count 2\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Waitlisted with position value 3, and the session's waitlist count value is 3\",\n      \"when\": \"joinWaitlist(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session that overlaps a session Alex has Booked, and Alex holds 10 upcoming Booked sessions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Waitlisted and no error is returned\",\n      \"when\": \"joinWaitlist(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with free spots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"spots available\\\" and the waitlist count value is unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"joinWaitlist(session) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex joins the waitlist of a full Scheduled session that starts within the booking window, the booking service shall create a Waitlisted record whose position equals the previous waitlist count plus 1 and increase the waitlist count by 1, without checking the overlap rule or the 10-booking limit.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Sessions starting exactly 168 hours and 168 hours plus 1 minute after now, each with free spots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The first call returns a Booked record and the second returns the \\\"outside booking window\\\" error\",\n      \"when\": \"book is called for each\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Sessions starting exactly 15 minutes and 14 minutes after now, each with free spots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The first call returns a Booked record and the second returns the \\\"outside booking window\\\" error\",\n      \"when\": \"book is called for each\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session starting 169 hours after now\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"outside booking window\\\" and the waitlist count value is unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"joinWaitlist is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If a session starts more than 7×24 hours after now or less than 15 minutes after now, then the booking service shall reject book and join-waitlist requests with a \\\"outside booking window\\\" error.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"Q-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session that started 1 minute ago with free spots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"class has started\\\" and no record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"book(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex holds a Booked record on a session that started 1 minute ago\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"class has started\\\" and the record status value stays Booked\",\n      \"when\": \"cancel(booking) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session that started 1 minute ago\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-10.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"class has started\\\" and the waitlist count is unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"joinWaitlist(session) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If a session's start time is at or before now, then the booking service shall reject book, join-waitlist and cancel requests for it with a \\\"class has started\\\" error.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\" and free spots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"cancelled by studio\\\" and no record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"book(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session with status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\"\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"cancelled by studio\\\" and the waitlist count is unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"joinWaitlist(session) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If a session has status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\", then the booking service shall reject book and join-waitlist requests for it with a \\\"cancelled by studio\\\" error.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked for \\\"Power HIIT\\\" 18:00–18:45 on a day\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error message is \\\"You're already booked for Power HIIT at 18:00–18:45.\\\" and no record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"book is called for an 18:30 Spin session the same day\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked for \\\"Power HIIT\\\" 18:00–18:45 on a day\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Booked\",\n      \"when\": \"book is called for a session starting at 18:45 the same day\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If a book request would give Alex two Booked sessions whose time ranges overlap, then the booking service shall reject it with an error naming the conflicting session and its time range, while sessions that only touch end-to-start are not treated as overlapping.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"ASM-7\",\n     \"ASM-18\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex holds 10 upcoming Booked sessions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error message is \\\"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\\\" and the Booked count stays 10\",\n      \"when\": \"book is called for an 11th bookable session\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex holds 9 upcoming Booked sessions and 1 Waitlisted session\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Booked\",\n      \"when\": \"book is called for a bookable session\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex already holds 10 upcoming Booked sessions, then the booking service shall reject a book request with the error \\\"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\\\"\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Booked record on a session starting in exactly 2 hours with booked count 16 and waitlist count 2\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Cancelled and late flag false, the booked count value stays 16 and the waitlist count value is 1\",\n      \"when\": \"cancel(booking) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Booked record on a session starting in 3 hours with booked count 10 and waitlist count 0\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booked count value is 9\",\n      \"when\": \"cancel(booking) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex cancels a Booked record at least 2 hours before the session starts, the booking service shall set the record status to Cancelled with the late flag false, and shall reduce the session's waitlist count by 1 if it is above 0 or otherwise reduce the booked count by 1.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Booked record on a session starting in 90 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Cancelled and late flag true\",\n      \"when\": \"cancel(booking) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Booked record on a session starting in 1 hour 59 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned value is true, and for a session starting in exactly 2 hours the returned value is false\",\n      \"when\": \"isLateCancellation(booking) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex cancels a Booked record less than 2 hours before the session starts, then the booking service shall set the record status to Cancelled with the late flag true and apply the same count changes as a free cancellation.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-7\",\n     \"ASM-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted at position 3 on a session with waitlist count 3\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status Cancelled and late flag false, and the session's waitlist count value is 2\",\n      \"when\": \"leaveWaitlist(booking) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex leaves a waitlist, the booking service shall set the Waitlisted record status to Cancelled with the late flag false and reduce the session's waitlist count by 1.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session with booked count 16, waitlist count 2, and Alex Waitlisted at position 1 with no overlap and fewer than 10 Booked sessions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's returned record has status Booked, the booked count value stays 16 and the waitlist count value is 1\",\n      \"when\": \"simulateOtherMemberCancellation(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session with waitlist count 3 and Alex Waitlisted at position 2\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's returned record is Waitlisted with position value 1 and the waitlist count value is 2\",\n      \"when\": \"simulateOtherMemberCancellation(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session with booked count 16 and waitlist count 0\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booked count value is 15\",\n      \"when\": \"simulateOtherMemberCancellation(session) is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the test-only hook simulateOtherMemberCancellation(session) runs, the booking service shall promote the first waitlisted member, changing Alex's record to Booked if Alex is at position 1 and eligible, otherwise moving Alex's waitlist position up by 1, and shall reduce the waitlist count by 1 with booked count unchanged, or reduce the booked count by 1 when the waitlist is empty.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"ASM-16\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted at position 1 on a full session with waitlist count 2 that overlaps Alex's Booked \\\"Power HIIT\\\"\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's returned record has status Waitlisted, position value 1 and a reason field naming \\\"Power HIIT\\\", and the waitlist count value is 1\",\n      \"when\": \"simulateOtherMemberCancellation(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted at position 1 and holds 10 upcoming Booked sessions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's returned record stays Waitlisted at position 1 with a reason field stating the 10-class limit\",\n      \"when\": \"simulateOtherMemberCancellation(session) is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex's record has a stored promotion-skipped reason\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-18.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The reason text is displayed next to \\\"You're #1 on the waitlist\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"The Class Detail screen for that session is opened\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If promoting Alex from waitlist position 1 would overlap another Booked session of Alex's, take Alex above 10 upcoming Booked sessions, or the session starts less than 15 minutes aft