 return Upcoming as the count of upcoming Booked records, Classes this month as the count of Attended records in the current Europe/London calendar month, and Current streak as the number of consecutive Monday–Sunday weeks with at least one Attended record.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-34\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"ASM-11\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Seeded data with today Wednesday 7 October\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-35.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"Rows are displayed in start-time order under day headings such as \\\"Today\\\", \\\"Tomorrow\\\" and \\\"Fri 9 Oct\\\", each with a \\\"Booked\\\" or \\\"Waitlisted #N\\\" badge and a Cancel or Leave button\",\n      \"when\": \"The My Bookings Upcoming tab is shown\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex late-cancelled a class\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-35.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"That row is displayed with the badge \\\"Late cancel\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"The Past tab is shown\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A My Bookings row\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-35.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The Class Detail screen for that session is shown\",\n      \"when\": \"The row is activated\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The My Bookings screen shall show a header with avatar, name and membership, the three stat tiles, and Upcoming and Past tabs, where Upcoming lists Booked and Waitlisted records by start time grouped as \\\"Today\\\", \\\"Tomorrow\\\" or \\\"Thu 15 Oct\\\" with a Cancel or Leave action, and Past lists Attended and Cancelled records most recent first with a status badge reading \\\"Attended\\\", \\\"Cancelled\\\" or \\\"Late cancel\\\".\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-35\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-7\",\n     \"ASM-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex has no Booked or Waitlisted upcoming records\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-36.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The text \\\"No upcoming classes\\\" was displayed and the Schedule screen is now shown\",\n      \"when\": \"\\\"Browse schedule\\\" on the Upcoming tab is activated\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"While Alex has no upcoming records or no past records, the My Bookings screen shall show \\\"No upcoming classes\\\" with a \\\"Browse schedule\\\" button that opens Schedule, or \\\"Your class history will appear here.\\\", respectively.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-36\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"simulateOtherMemberCancellation promoted Alex on \\\"Power HIIT\\\" while the app was closed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-37.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"A toast containing \\\"Power HIIT\\\" is displayed once and is not shown again on the next reload\",\n      \"when\": \"The app is opened\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the app opens after Alex was promoted from a waitlist since the last visit, the booking app shall show a toast naming the class Alex is now booked for.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-37\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The OS set to dark mode\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-38.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"Each screen is shown with a dark background and every text/background pair measured by an automated contrast checker reports a ratio value of at least 4.5:1 for body text\",\n      \"when\": \"Each of the three screens is opened\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A design reviewer\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-38.2\",\n      \"level\": \"manual\",\n      \"then\": \"The reviewer records that class type accents match the named colours consistently and the look is boutique rather than an admin template\",\n      \"when\": \"The three screens are reviewed in light and dark mode at 375 px and 1280 px\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking app shall define its colours as design tokens with a warm off-white background, near-black text, one brand primary, accents Yoga sage green, Pilates dusty rose, HIIT coral/orange, Spin electric blue and Boxing deep plum used on tags, card edges and the detail hero, and a dark theme applied when the system prefers dark mode.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-38\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with capacity 20 and 14 booked\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-39.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The value read is \\\"6 of 20 spots left\\\"\",\n      \"when\": \"Its capacity bar's accessible name is read by an accessibility tree inspector\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The cancel confirmation dialog is open\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-39.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"Focus stays on dialog controls during tabbing, and after Escape the dialog is no longer shown and focus is on the Cancel booking button\",\n      \"when\": \"Tab is pressed repeatedly and then Escape\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A keyboard-only user\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-39.3\",\n      \"level\": \"manual\",\n      \"then\": \"Every step is completed without a pointer and a focus outline is shown on each focused control\",\n      \"when\": \"They filter by Yoga, book a class and cancel it from My Bookings\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking app shall be fully operable by keyboard with visible focus, use semantic headings, landmarks and labels, announce the capacity bar as \\\"N of M spots left\\\", pair every colour signal with text or an icon, and trap focus in dialogs that close on Escape.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-39\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Viewports of 360 px and 375 px wide\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-40.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The page's scroll width value equals the viewport width (only the day strip scrolls horizontally)\",\n      \"when\": \"Each of the three screens is opened\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A 1280 px wide viewport\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-40.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"Class Detail is shown as a side panel while the schedule list stays displayed\",\n      \"when\": \"A class card is activated\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A 360 px wide viewport\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-40.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"Each measured width and height value is at least 44 px\",\n      \"when\": \"The bounding box of every button, chip and link is measured\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking app shall render without horizontal page scrolling from 360 px wide, show schedule cards in 2 columns from 768 px, and from 1024 px show Class Detail as a side panel beside the schedule within a maximum content width, with every interactive target at least 44 × 44 px.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-40\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\",\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"ASM-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The repository with dependencies installed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-41.1\",\n      \"level\": \"job\",\n      \"then\": \"The test report lists at least one passing test for each of the 8 named business rules and one passing end-to-end test, with a failed count of 0\",\n      \"when\": \"The test job is run\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the project's automated test job runs, the test suite shall run passing tests for booking success, full-class rejection with waitlist join, waitlist promotion, the 7-day and 15-minute windows, the late-cancellation flag, overlap rejection, the 10-booking limit, and past and studio-cancelled rejection, plus an end-to-end test that filters by Yoga, books a class, finds it in My Bookings and cancels it.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-41\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"suggestions\": [\n   \"Add a storage version key so future seed or schema changes can migrate or reset local storage cleanly.\",\n   \"Add a dev-only 'reset demo data' option to make manual QA and demos repeatable.\",\n   \"Consider an ARIA live region announcing toast messages so screen-reader users hear booking confirmations and Undo.\",\n   \"Consider guarding against two open tabs writing to local storage at once (storage event sync) to avoid lost bookings.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d2\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"All business rules live in one booking module (ASM-6) that takes an injectable clock, so unit tests can set 'now'. Every screen action goes through this module.\",\n   \"ASM-21: Filters inside one group (type, intensity, time of day) are OR'd and filters across groups are AND'd. Intensity is multi-select like class type.\",\n   \"ASM-22: 'Classes this month' counts only Attended bookings. Current streak counts consecutive Monday–Sunday weeks with at least one Attended booking, counting back from the current week; if the current week has none yet, counting starts at the previous week. This comes from request §13.\",\n   \"ASM-23: The disabled-footer reason texts are 'Class has started', 'Cancelled by studio' and 'Booking opens 7 days before class' / 'Booking closes 15 minutes before class'.\",\n   \"ASM-24: Request §13 says a waitlist promotion is announced in-app with a toast the next time the app is opened.\",\n   \"Card availability labels: 'N spots left' when more than 3 are left, 'Only N left' when 2–3 are left, and '1 spot left' when 1 is left. The last one follows the §11 booking example even though it differs from the §6 'Only N left' pattern.\",\n   \"Seeded past Attended bookings for Alex may point to sessions dated before the current week, so history exists whatever day of the week the app is first loaded. These sessions don't appear on the Schedule.\",\n   \"Leaving a waitlist stores the booking as Cancelled with no late flag.\",\n   \"Seeded bookings skip the booking-window checks.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"Time from day selection to cards painted ≤ 1000 ms at the 95th percentile over 10 runs\",\n    \"text\": \"The Schedule for a selected day renders with seed data on a mid-range phone (Chrome DevTools 4× CPU throttle, Moto G Power profile).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"Visual change on screen ≤ 100 ms after the tap in 95% of 20 measured taps\",\n    \"text\": \"Booking, cancel, join and leave actions give visual feedback through an optimistic update.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n    \"metric\": \"Contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 for normal text and ≥ 3:1 for large text and UI components on 100% of token pairs checked\",\n    \"text\": \"Text and UI colours meet WCAG 2.1 AA in both light and dark themes.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n    \"metric\": \"100% of tappable targets ≥ 44×44 CSS px at a 360 px viewport\",\n    \"text\": \"Interactive controls are large enough to tap.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n    \"metric\": \"0 horizontal page scroll at viewport widths 360, 375, 768, 1024 and 1440 px on all three screens\",\n    \"text\": \"No horizontal page scrolling on supported widths.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n    \"metric\": \"0 duplicate booking records after 10 rapid taps on Book for one session\",\n    \"text\": \"Repeated taps on Book never create duplicate bookings.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n    \"metric\": \"0 stack traces or raw exception messages shown across all error states in the test suite\",\n    \"text\": \"Users never see raw errors.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n    \"metric\": \"All acceptance criteria pass on the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox (8 browser versions)\",\n    \"text\": \"Supported browsers (ASM-12).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n    \"metric\": \"Deployed to exactly 1 cloud region\",\n    \"text\": \"Hosting (ASM-13) as a static site in the client's cloud account.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n    \"metric\": \"0 outbound network requests containing booking or member data during the end-to-end test\",\n    \"text\": \"Member data (name, bookings) stays in the browser (PII).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n    \"metric\": \"Median time from app open to booked ≤ 30 seconds across 5 usability test participants\",\n    \"text\": \"Members can find and book a class quickly.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"Sign in, sign up and password reset (one demo member is pre-signed-in)\",\n   \"Payments, credits, class packs and membership purchase\",\n   \"Staff, instructor or admin screens and schedule editing, including the studio cancelling a class that Alex holds (ASM-8)\",\n   \"Email, SMS and push notifications\",\n   \"Calendar export or sync\",\n   \"Multiple studio locations\",\n   \"Native mobile apps\",\n   \"Multi-language support\",\n   \"A backend server or database: persistence is browser local storage only (ASM-15)\",\n   \"Any visible UI for the waitlist promotion demo hook (ASM-16)\",\n   \"Browsing schedule weeks beyond the current and next week (ASM-9, ASM-20)\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A fresh browser with no stored app data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The Schedule screen is displayed with the 'Pulse Studio' wordmark and an 'AR' avatar in the top bar, and no sign-in page is shown\",\n      \"when\": \"The user opens the app root URL\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The Schedule screen is displayed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The My Bookings screen is displayed showing the name 'Alex Rivera' and membership 'Unlimited Monthly'\",\n      \"when\": \"The user activates the 'AR' avatar\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Pulse Studio app shall provide exactly three screens (Schedule as the home screen, Class Detail, and My Bookings) for the single pre-signed-in member Alex Rivera, with no sign-in screen.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The module clock is set to 2026-07-01T23:30Z (00:30 on 2 July in London)\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned value is 2026-07-02\",\n      \"when\": \"The test asks the booking module for today's date\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session starting at 2026-07-02T17:00Z\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned value is '18:00'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads the session's formatted start time from the booking module\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking module shall work out 'today', day boundaries and every time-based rule in the Europe/London timezone and return times formatted as 24-hour HH:mm.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Empty storage and the module clock set to Wednesday 2026-10-07 10:00 Europe/London\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned session list has at least 40 records, all starting between Monday 2026-10-05 00:00 and Sunday 2026-10-18 23:59 (except sessions for Alex's past bookings), covering the types Yoga, Pilates, HIIT, Spin and Boxing and the rooms Studio A, Studio B and Spin Room\",\n      \"when\": \"The booking module initialises\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The seed data generated in AC-3.1\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The instructor count is 5, the count of sessions with booked count equal to capacity is at least 3, the count of sessions with 1–3 spots left is at least 3, and the count of sessions with status 'Cancelled by studio' is at least 1\",\n      \"when\": \"The test counts sessions and instructors\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The seed data generated in AC-3.1\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned list has exactly 2 Booked bookings on future sessions, 1 Waitlisted booking with a waitlist position field, and 3 Attended bookings on past sessions, and no booking references a 'Cancelled by studio' session\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads Alex's bookings\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Each seeded session\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Each record has a name, type, intensity (Low/Medium/High), instructor with name, bio and avatar, room, start, duration in {30,45,60,75}, capacity, booked count, waitlist count, a description, a what-to-bring list and a status\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads its fields\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the app loads with no stored data, the booking module shall generate seed data for the current and next Monday–Sunday weeks in Europe/London, worked out from the load date, containing at least 40 class sessions across all 5 class types and all 3 rooms, 5 instructors, at least 3 full sessions, at least 3 sessions with 1–3 spots left, at least 1 session with status 'Cancelled by studio', and for Alex 2 upcoming Booked bookings, 1 Waitlisted booking and 3 past Attended bookings, none of them on a studio-cancelled session.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"ASM-5\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-20\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex books session S through a booking module instance\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The new instance returns a Booked record for S and S's booked count value is the same as after the booking\",\n      \"when\": \"A new booking module instance is created over the same local storage\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Seed data was generated on first load on 2026-10-07\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned session list has the same session IDs and start times as before and is not regenerated\",\n      \"when\": \"A new booking module instance is created over the same storage with the clock set to 2026-10-09\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex has booked a class in the app\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The class is shown in the Upcoming list with a 'Booked' badge\",\n      \"when\": \"The user reloads the browser page and opens My Bookings\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking module shall store bookings, session counts and the generated seed data in browser local storage so that they are unchanged after a page reload.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-15\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Session 'Sunrise Vinyasa' with capacity 20, booked count 18, starting in 2 days, and Alex has no conflicting bookings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Booked', a non-empty ID and a created date/time, and the session's booked count value is 19\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the booking module's book operation for that session\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex books a Scheduled session that has spots left and passes every booking rule, the booking module shall create a Booked booking with an ID and created date/time and increase the session's booked count by 1.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Session 'Power HIIT' with capacity 12 and booked count 12\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'full', no booking record is created, and the booked count value stays 12\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation for it\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex tries to book a session whose booked count equals its capacity, then the booking module shall reject the booking with a 'class full' error and leave the counts unchanged.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with spots that starts in 167 hours 59 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Booked'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with spots that starts in 168 hours 1 minute\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'outside-booking-window' and no booking record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with spots that starts in exactly 15 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Booked'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with spots that starts in 14 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-7.4\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'outside-booking-window' and no booking record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex tries to book a session that starts more than 7×24 hours from now or less than 15 minutes from now, then the booking module shall reject the booking with an error naming the booking window.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session that started 5 minutes ago with spots left\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'started' and no booking record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex holds a Booked booking on a session that started 10 minutes ago\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'started' and the booking status value is still 'Booked'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the cancel operation for that booking\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with status 'Cancelled by studio' starting tomorrow\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Both calls return an error with code 'cancelled-by-studio' and no booking record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation and then the join-waitlist operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex tries to book, cancel, join the waitlist for or leave the waitlist for a session that has already started, or to book or join the waitlist for a session with status 'Cancelled by studio', then the booking module shall reject the action with an error naming the reason and leave all bookings and counts unchanged.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked on 'Power HIIT' 18:00–18:45 today and a Spin session starts at 18:30 the same day with spots left\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'overlap' and message \\\"You're already booked for Power HIIT at 18:00–18:45.\\\", and no booking record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation for the Spin session\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked on a session 18:00–18:45 and another session starts at 18:45 the same day with spots left\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Booked'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation for the 18:45 session\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex tries to book a session whose time overlaps one of Alex's Booked sessions, then the booking module shall reject the booking with the error message \\\"You're already booked for <class name> at <start>–<end>.\\\", where sessions that only touch end-to-start do not count as overlapping.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"ASM-7\",\n     \"ASM-18\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex holds 10 Booked bookings on future, non-overlapping sessions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'limit' and message \\\"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\\\", and the count of Alex's Booked records stays 10\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation for an 11th eligible session\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex holds 9 Booked bookings on future sessions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Booked'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation for a 10th eligible session\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex already holds 10 Booked bookings on sessions that have not started, then the booking module shall reject a further booking with the error message \\\"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\\\"\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex has just booked session S and its booked count is 19\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Both calls return an error with code 'already-booked', the count of Alex's booking records for S is 1, and the booked count value stays 19\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the book operation for S again twice\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If Alex already holds a Booked or Waitlisted booking on a session, then the booking module shall reject a further book or join-waitlist call for that session without creating a booking or changing counts.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"'Power HIIT' is full with waitlist count 2 and starts tomorrow\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Waitlisted' and waitlist position 3, and the session's waitlist count value is 3\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the join-waitlist operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex holds 10 upcoming Booked bookings, one of which overlaps a full session F starting tomorrow\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Waitlisted'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the join-waitlist operation for F\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session starting in 10 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'outside-booking-window' and the waitlist count value is unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the join-waitlist operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A session with spots left\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-12.4\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned error has code 'not-full' and no booking record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the join-waitlist operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex joins the waitlist for a full Scheduled session that starts within 7×24 hours and at least 15 minutes from now, the booking module shall create a Waitlisted booking with position equal to the previous waitlist count plus 1 and increase the waitlist count by 1, without checking overlap or the 10-booking limit.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted #3 on a session with waitlist count 3 starting tomorrow\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking status is 'Cancelled' with late flag false, the waitlist count value is 2, and Alex's upcoming list no longer contains the session\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the leave-waitlist operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex leaves the waitlist for a session that has not started, the booking module shall set that booking's status to Cancelled with no late flag, remove it from Alex's upcoming list and decrease the session's waitlist count by 1.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked on a session starting in exactly 2 hours\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Cancelled' and late flag value false\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the cancel operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex cancels a Booked booking at least 2 hours before the session starts, the booking module shall set its status to Cancelled with the late flag false.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked on a session starting in 90 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned booking has status 'Cancelled' and late flag value true\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the cancel operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex cancels a Booked booking less than 2 hours before the session starts, the booking module shall set its status to Cancelled with the late flag true.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-7\",\n     \"ASM-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked on a session with capacity 12, booked count 12 and waitlist count 4\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The session's booked count value is 12 and waitlist count value is 3\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the cancel operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked on a session with booked count 8 and waitlist count 0\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The session's booked count value is 7 and waitlist count value is 0\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the cancel operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex cancels a Booked booking, the booking module shall keep the session's booked count the same and decrease its waitlist count by 1 if the waitlist count is above 0, and otherwise decrease the booked count by 1.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session starting tomorrow with booked count 12, waitlist count 3, Alex Waitlisted #1, and no overlap or limit problem for Alex\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's booking status value is 'Booked', the waitlist count value is 2 and the booked count value is 12\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the promotion hook for that session\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A full session with waitlist count 3 and Alex Waitlisted #2\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's booking status is still 'Waitlisted' with position value 1, and the waitlist count value is 2\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the promotion hook for that session\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the tests-only promotion hook simulates another booked member cancelling a session on which Alex is Waitlisted #1 and Alex is eligible, the booking module shall set Alex's booking status to Booked, decrease the waitlist count by 1 and keep the booked count the same.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"ASM-16\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted #1 on a full Spin session 18:30–19:15 with waitlist count 3, and Booked on 'Power HIIT' 18:00–18:45 the same day\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's booking status is 'Waitlisted' with position 1, the waitlist count value is 2, and the returned result has reason 'overlap' naming 'Power HIIT'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the promotion hook for the Spin session\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted #1 on a full session and holds 10 upcoming Booked bookings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's booking status is 'Waitlisted' with position 1 and the returned result has reason 'limit'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the promotion hook\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted #1 on a full session starting in 10 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-18.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's booking status is 'Waitlisted' with position 1 and the returned result has reason 'outside-booking-window'\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the promotion hook\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If the promotion hook fires for a session on which Alex is Waitlisted #1 and promoting Alex would overlap another of Alex's Booked sessions, exceed 10 upcoming Booked sessions, or the session starts within 15 minutes, then the booking module shall keep Alex Waitlisted at position 1, decrease the waitlist count by 1 to stand for the next member being promoted, and return the reason.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"ASM-2\",\n     \"ASM-14\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex has just booked a session starting in 1 hour (inside the 2-hour window), raising its booked count from 18 to 19\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"Alex's booking list contains no record for the session (neither Booked nor Cancelled) and the booked count value is 18\",\n      \"when\": \"The test calls the undo-booking operation for that booking\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When Alex undoes a booking from the booking toast, the booking module shall remove that booking as if it was never made, with no Cancelled record, no late flag and the session's booked count restored.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"Q-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex is Booked on a session 07:00–08:00 today and the clock is set to 08:00\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status 'Attended' and is in the Past list, not the Upcoming list\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads Alex's bookings\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The same booking and the clock set to 07:59\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned record has status 'Booked' and is in the Upcoming list\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads Alex's bookings\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a session on which Alex holds a Booked booking has ended, the booking module shall report that booking with status Attended and list it under Past.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"Q-8\",\n     \"ASM-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A day with Yoga at 07:00, HIIT at 12:00, Yoga at 16:59 and Spin at 17:00\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned list is the 07:00 and 16:59 Yoga sessions in that order\",\n      \"when\": \"The test requests that day with type filter [Yoga]\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The same day\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-21.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned list contains only the 17:00 Spin session\",\n      \"when\": \"The test requests time-of-day filter [Evening]\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The same day\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-21.3\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned list is the 12:00 HIIT and 16:59 Yoga sessions\",\n      \"when\": \"The test requests time-of-day filter [Afternoon] and type filter [HIIT, Yoga]\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The same day\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-21.4\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned list has all 4 sessions ordered by start time\",\n      \"when\": \"The test requests no filters\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the schedule is asked for a day with filters, the booking module shall return that day's sessions ordered by start time, matching any selected class type, any selected intensity and any selected time of day (Morning before 12:00, Afternoon 12:00–16:59, Evening 17:00 onward), with no selection in a group meaning no restriction.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"ASM-10\",\n     \"ASM-21\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The clock is Tue 13 Oct 2026 09:00 and Alex is Booked today 18:00, Waitlisted tomorrow 07:00 and Booked Thu 15 Oct 12:00\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned groups are 'Today', 'Tomorrow', 'Thu 15 Oct' in that order, each holding the matching booking\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads the Upcoming list\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex has Attended bookings on 5 Oct and 9 Oct and a late Cancelled booking on 12 Oct\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-22.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned list order is 12 Oct, 9 Oct, 5 Oct and the 12 Oct record has late flag true\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads the Past list\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The booking module shall return Alex's Upcoming list as Booked and Waitlisted bookings on sessions not yet started, ordered by start time and grouped under 'Today', 'Tomorrow' or a 'Thu 15 Oct' style label, and the Past list as Attended and Cancelled bookings, most recent first.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Alex has 2 upcoming Booked and 1 Waitlisted bookings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-23.1\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The Upcoming value is 2\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads the stats\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The clock is 20 Oct 2026, Alex has 3 Attended bookings in October, 1 in September and 1 late-cancelled booking in October\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-23.2\",\n      \"level\": \"unit\",\n      \"then\": \"The Classes this month value is 3\",\n      \"when\": \"The test reads the stats\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The clock is Wed in week W, Alex has Attended bookings in weeks W, W-1 and W-2